NAMING_VS_MECHANISM: NAMING ONLY. The L1 empirically dissolves the one distinction the claim staked
its novelty on — "gate on live-window content vs gate on past queries (cache)." At matched skip-rate
they capture the SAME redundant retrievals at equal Pareto efficiency (F1 Δ ~0). So "live-window
residency gate" is a rename of semantic query caching, not a new mechanism. The remaining axis
(in-context vs parametric self-knowledge) is already occupied by A-RAG's Context Tracker.

FATAL_COLLISIONS:
- N1 (operational): in-context gate ≡ semantic query cache (GPTCache) on real data → the narrow
  mechanism delta is measurement-zero. Verifiable via the L1's own pre-registered result.
- N4 (prior-art): A-RAG Context Tracker already gates retrieval on read/in-context residency
  (packet-sourced; corroborated in spirit by "To Retrieve or To Think?" 2601.08747).
- Both pre-registered kill-branches fired as designed. The mechanism novelty is dead two ways.

